            <section class="fade-in">
                <h2>What I Care About</h2>
                <p>
                    I like software that is simple without being simplistic: APIs that are clear, interfaces
                    that are inclusive, systems that can evolve, and code that the next developer can
                    understand without a heroic amount of archaeology.
                </p>
                <p>
                    TerraPDF grew from that same point of view. It is built around a fluent API, practical
                    document layout, and a zero-dependency C# implementation that developers can understand,
                    ship, and trust.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="fade-in delay-100">
                <h2>TerraPDF</h2>
                <p>
                    I created TerraPDF to make professional PDF generation in .NET feel direct and dependable.
                    It supports layouts, tables, images, links, bookmarks, vector graphics, WinAnsi text, and
                    AES-128 PDF encryption without native binaries or third-party runtime packages.
                </p>
                <p>
                    You can explore the library at
                    <a href="https://terrapdf.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">terrapdf.com</a>,
                    install it from <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/TerraPDF/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NuGet</a>,
                    or view the source on <a href="https://github.com/sahebansari/TerraPDF" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
                </p>
            </section>

